# The transcript's one line a machine decides: the thermometer's, on its serial port.
line: serial: the thermometer on a pseudo-terminal at 9600 baud answered 22 queries and left 7 unanswered, 0 refused
or: serial: skipped: no pseudo-terminal on this system (unsupported); the thermometer's 22 readings handed in
why: the thermometer stands on a pseudo-terminal pair, which `serial.open_pseudo` makes on Darwin and Linux and refuses `unsupported` on Windows; there the demo hands the monitor the readings the thermometer would have answered, and its silence once they are spent, so every other line is the same
